    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that it's \"complex,\" but it feels like a bit of a cop-out. if you had to weigh the two, isn't it true that a small business owner is usually just trying to survive thin margins, whereas the arguments for higher wages are often more about social ideals than actual economic reality? like, can a local cafe really afford to bake those \"ideals\" into its payroll without going under?",
